--
--   **Context.** KFZ Pass: list moves, conjugate copies and record replication (uniform counts)
--
--   All counts are run-time data (`rptX`, the count copied from a register). Every spec is
--   frame-preserving: only the named stacks change.
--
--   * **`mvX_runs`**: move `L` from `X` to `Y` (reversed); **`mv2_runs`**: move through `pU`
--     (order kept); **`dropX_runs`**: drop `L`.
--   * **`cnjCp_runs`**: push the conjugate of the Gaussian list on `H` onto `W` (order kept), `H`
--     unchanged; counts `2N` on `nX2`, `N` on `nX`.
--   * **`replP_runs`**: push `N` copies of the Gaussian list on `H` onto `W`; counts `N` on `rN`,
